"""Summarize the renderer A/B measurements without implying native GPU results."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
from statistics import median
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
results=root/'rendering'
data={'session':{},'render':{},'replays':[]}
for mode in ('baseline','retained'):
    bench=json.loads((results/mode/'results-bare.json').read_text())
    replay=json.loads((results/mode/'results-replay-60.json').read_text())
    bucket=replay['renderProfile']['render']
    data['session'][mode]=median(row['elapsedMs'] for row in bench['benchmarks'])
    data['render'][mode]=bucket['ms']/bucket['count']
for mode,rate in [('baseline',60),('retained',60),('retained',240),('retained-reception',240)]:
    result=json.loads((results/mode/f'results-replay-{rate}.json').read_text())
    sample=result['samples'][0]
    data['replays'].append({'mode':mode,'target':rate,'scene':sample['sceneUpdates'],'ui':sample['uiUpdates']})
(results/'summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
template='''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>
body{margin:0;color:var(--foreground);font:14px/1.55 var(--font-sans,system-ui)}h2{font-size:20px;line-height:1.3;margin:0 0 10px}p{margin:10px 0}.muted{color:var(--muted-foreground)}.panel{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius,10px);padding:16px;margin:16px 0}.row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:65px 1fr 72px;gap:10px;align-items:center;margin:20px 0}.track{background:var(--muted);height:18px;border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden}.bar{height:18px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px}.card{padding:16px;background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius,10px)}strong.metric{display:block;font-size:24px}select{max-width:100%;color:var(--foreground);background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:5px;padding:7px;font:inherit}.small{font-size:12px}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:12px}th,td{text-align:left;padding:9px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}th{color:var(--muted-foreground);font-weight:400}a{color:var(--primary)}@media(max-width:430px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}.row{grid-template-columns:57px 1fr 65px;gap:7px}}
</style></head><body>
<h2>3D rendering has removable work; the 60 FPS ceiling still needs isolation</h2>
<p>Your active 240 target rules out the old scene limit. A smaller window making no difference points toward CPU/runtime work, but does not identify the dominant cost on your machine.</p>
<div class="panel"><strong>Applied: keep scene objects attached between draws</strong><p>The old renderer detached and reattached character trees on every update. The shared replacement preserves attachment, reconciles draw order and removes objects only when needed.</p><label for="metric">Measurement </label><select id="metric"><option value="render">Real replay · AS3 render-call time</option><option value="session">Synthetic session redraw loop</option></select><div role="img" id="chart"><div class="row"><span>Former</span><div class="track"><div class="bar" style="width:100%;background:#d5a85c"></div></div><strong id="before"></strong></div><div class="row"><span>Retained</span><div class="track"><div class="bar" id="bar" style="background:#55bfa8"></div></div><strong id="after"></strong></div></div><p id="scope" class="small muted"></p></div>
<p><strong>This is not a fourfold gameplay FPS gain.</strong> Whole-probe frame events rose only from 5.33/s to 5.53/s on this software-rendered host. Substantial animation, drawing and scheduling costs remain outside the optimized loop. No RTX/Wine speedup is claimed.</p>
<div class="cards"><div class="card"><strong class="metric">83.3 ms</strong>Time per frame at your reported 12 FPS</div><div class="card"><strong class="metric">4.17 ms</strong>Total frame budget needed for 240 FPS</div></div>
<p>240 is permitted by the game policy. Reaching it requires both a runtime/presentation path that runs above 60 and enough performance for every frame. A 240 Hz display and fast GPU alone do not establish either.</p>
<details><summary>Correctness checks passed</summary><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Target</th><th>Scene / UI updates</th><th>Completion</th></tr></thead><tbody id="replays"></tbody></table></div><p class="small muted">Ordering, object removal/reappearance, duplicate draws, pooled shape layers and unchanged cached frames passed. Both client roots compiled; shared smoke passed in both runtime-policy branches inside Ruffle.</p></details>
<div class="panel"><strong>Next: a blank probe through your exact Wine launcher</strong><p>If it also stays near 60 with a 240 target, investigate Flash/Wine/XWayland independently of the game scene. If it runs above 60, compare game UI and running-player workloads.</p><p class="small muted">The launcher currently forces Wine's X11 driver, so your Wayland session uses XWayland. This is a diagnostic boundary, not proof of the cause. The probe starts no game or backend and changes no saved game preferences.</p></div>
<p class="small muted">Measurements: Chromium/Ruffle, SwiftShader software GPU. One real replay capture per variant; three session-loop samples each. Wine and physical 240 Hz presentation remain untested here. The <a href="https://airsdk.dev/reference/actionscript/3.0/flash/display/Stage.html#frameRate">Stage reference</a> distinguishes a requested rate from platform capability.</p>
<script>const data=__DATA__;function draw(){const key=document.getElementById('metric').value,values=data[key];document.getElementById('before').textContent=values.baseline.toFixed(key==='render'?1:0)+' ms';document.getElementById('after').textContent=values.retained.toFixed(key==='render'?1:0)+' ms';document.getElementById('bar').style.width=(100*values.retained/values.baseline)+'%';document.getElementById('chart').setAttribute('aria-label',key+': '+values.baseline.toFixed(1)+' to '+values.retained.toFixed(1)+' milliseconds');document.getElementById('scope').textContent=key==='render'?'Average of 70 View3D.render calls in one ten-runner replay per variant: about 29% less measured AS3 render-call time. This excludes later Flash drawing/composition.':'Median of three samples, each 300 draws of ten synthetic character trees with 30 children each: about 75% less session-loop time.'}document.getElementById('metric').onchange=draw;draw();for(const result of data.replays){const tr=document.createElement('tr');for(const value of [result.mode.includes('reception')?'Pass/catch':result.mode==='baseline'?'Ten runners · former':'Ten runners · retained',result.target,result.scene+' / '+result.ui,'Once, ordered']){const td=document.createElement('td');td.textContent=value;tr.append(td)}document.getElementById('replays').append(tr)}</script></body></html>'''
(root/'renderer-report.html').write_text(template.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data)))
print(json.dumps({'report':str(root/'renderer-report.html'),'replays':len(data['replays'])}))
